# Private / AI-agent files — keep off GitHub
# NOTE: CLAUDE.md and rules/ are intentionally tracked — the test gate reads them
# (test-count / Protocol 38 / Protocol 40 guards), so they must stay in the repo.
.claude/

# Codex's local agent files — same reasoning as .claude/ above, and this repo is
# PUBLIC. AGENTS.md here is a local, machine-generated Claude->Codex substitution of
# CLAUDE.md (it is NOT a second rulebook and nothing reads it); .codex/ holds local
# hook wiring. Neither is tracked, and both must stay out of the gate's `git add -A`.
AGENTS.md
.codex/

# Claude-facing local reference library (BRAIN_DUMP.md et al.) — local-only, never
# committed. It reconstructs a session's understanding from disk on the owner's PC;
# it is NOT for the phone (that is QUEUE.md — which since 2026-08-02 lives in the
# PRIVATE archive at _RobCo-Archive/!PLANNING/, not in this repo at all). See CLAUDE.md's
# pointer index. library/MANIFEST.txt is the one committed exception — a filename-only
# manifest (Protocol 46 / Suite 220) so the doc-reference-integrity gate can check
# pointer paths against it even on a clean CI checkout where library/ doesn't exist.
library/*
!library/MANIFEST.txt

# Generated PRIVATE phone-readable queue view (queue item L). The generator
# (scripts/queue-view.js) is tracked; its HTML output is regenerated on demand
# (npm run queue-view) and never committed — generation-over-maintenance, and it
# is not served/precached so there is no cache concern.
queue-view/

# Credential shapes — never committed. This repository is PUBLIC, and a pushed
# secret cannot be recalled: deleting it later leaves it in the history and in
# every clone, so the only cheap moment is before the first commit.
#
# Verified when these were added: no file of any of these shapes was tracked or
# present on disk, so this is preventive rather than a lid on an existing leak.
# That distinction matters — .gitignore has NO effect on a file that is already
# tracked, so a pattern added over a committed secret would look like a fix while
# changing nothing at all.
#
# The real credential store for this machine lives outside every repository by
# design, and nothing here should be read as making it safe to move one in.
.env
.env.*
# ...but a committed EXAMPLE is a normal thing to want, and it holds no values.
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.keystore
.netrc
id_rsa
id_rsa.*
id_ed25519
id_ed25519.*
*credentials.json
*-creds.json

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output
dist/
_site/
dist-staging/

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# IDE
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo

# Repomix output (generated artifact — never committed)
repomix-output.*

# CI failure-evidence (Health-batch U4) — screenshots + console/gate logs written
# ONLY when a check fails, uploaded by the CI workflow, then swept (Protocol 41).
# Never committed.
test-artifacts/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Local planning artifacts — never committed/pushed/deployed
# These are AI-agent research and design docs generated during the planning chain.
# They live in planning/ (the whole folder is ignored); the filename patterns
# below stay as a belt-and-suspenders guard in case any are kept/created elsewhere.
planning/
MASTER_PLAN.md
PARALLELIZATION_PLAN.md
HOUSE_STANDARD.md
DETERMINISTIC_FEATURES.md
*_AUDIT.md
*_SLATE.md
*_DESIGN.md
